From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: drm/simpledrm: software backlight for the J701F bootloader framebuffer

Written by Claude 2026-10-10 for the J701F project; not an upstream patch.
Applies on top of linux-sysfb-j701f-fast-argb-copy.patch. With the boolean
device-tree property "j701f,software-backlight" simpledrm registers the
backlight device "j701f-panel" (0-255) and reports its connector as DSI. The
level is applied to every pixel while the frame is copied to the framebuffer,
and a level change copies the current frame out again.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_helper.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/drm_sysfb_helper.h
@@ -80,6 +80,13 @@
 
 	/* hardware-framebuffer kernel address */
 	struct iosys_map fb_addr;
+
+	/*
+	 * J701F local: software backlight. When sw_backlight is set, the copy
+	 * into the framebuffer scales every pixel by sw_backlight_level / 255.
+	 */
+	bool sw_backlight;
+	unsigned int sw_backlight_level;
 };
 
 static inline struct drm_sysfb_device *to_drm_sysfb_device(struct drm_device *dev)
@@ -122,6 +129,8 @@
 #define DRM_SYSFB_PLANE_NFORMATS(_num_native) \
 	((_num_native) + 1)
 
